<title>AUSTRALIA: KLSE included on Australian approved exchange list.</title>
<headline>KLSE included on Australian approved exchange list.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australia's corporate regulator, the Australian Securities Commission (ASC), announced on Wednesday that the Kuala Lumpur Stock Exchange (KLSE) had been admitted to the list of ASC approved foreign exchanges.</p>
<p>This meant Australia's licensed securities dealers could now legally promote securities listed on the KLSE to their clients, the ASC said. The KLSE joins 14 others on the ASC approved list, including the London Stock Exchange, the New York Stock Exchange and Singapore Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
